<article class="env-lemma" id="0022">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0022">Lemma <span data-tag="0022">4.8.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $F, G, H : \mathcal{C}^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$ be functors. Let $a : F \to G$ and $b : H \to G$ be transformations of functors. Then the fibre product $F \times _{a, G, b} H$ in the category $\textit{PSh}(\mathcal{C})$ exists and is given by the formula </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (F \times _{a, G, b} H)(X) = F(X) \times _{a_ X, G(X), b_ X} H(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> for any object $X$ of $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>